  "seam": {
    "com/sulake/core/Core.as": "reached only for Core.crash() from EventDispatcherWrapper's error handler. Pulls the whole component runtime, the profiler and the AS3 SWF loader behind it",
    "com/sulake/core/assets/AssetLibraryCollection.as": "the AS3 asset registry, backed by LibraryLoader and FZip. SkyHaxe reads SWFs with SwfFile and keeps its own AssetLibrary",
    "com/sulake/habbo/avatar/AvatarAssetDownloadLibrary.as": "wraps LibraryLoader to fetch and unzip one hh_human_*.swf. SkyHaxe fetches the same bytes and reads them with SwfFile, so this is the download seam itself",
    "com/sulake/habbo/avatar/EffectAssetDownloadLibrary.as": "the same wrapper for effect libraries",
    "com/sulake/habbo/avatar/EffectAssetDownloadManager.as": "downloads optional effect libraries through AssetLoaderStruct. A standing avatar does not use an effect; SkyHaxe supplies a fail-closed no-effect seam until the effect asset path is implemented after the first visible avatar",
    "com/sulake/core/assets/IAssetLibrary.as": "declares its loader methods in terms of LibraryLoader, which is the remaining edge into the AS3 SWF loader. SkyHaxe has its own AssetLibrary, and the avatar code uses only the asset-lookup half of this interface",
    "com/sulake/habbo/avatar/AvatarRenderManager.as": "an IHabboComponent: its constructor, dependency wiring and configuration reads are all component-framework machinery the port does not have. Nothing in the closure calls more than two of its members -- events and isReady -- so the port supplies its own",
    "com/sulake/habbo/utils/HabboWebTools.as": "browser bridge for error reporting and navigation; ExternalInterface calls with no place in the port yet"
  },
  "note": "This is the generated avatar compositor plus the two room-user packet parsers that drive it. Package-at-a-time conversion cannot be ordered without this measured closure.",
